menu "PowerCanary"

    config CANARY_AC_PRESENT_MIN_V
        int "AC input voltage that counts as mains present (V)"
        default 50
        range 1 300
        help
            Mains counts as present only when the reported AC input voltage is
            at or above this value AND input current or power is non-zero.
            Voltage alone is not trusted: a DELTA 2 Max keeps reporting the
            last voltage it measured after its AC cord is pulled. The default
            suits both 120 V and 230 V systems.

    config CANARY_DEBOUNCE_S
        int "Seconds AC input must be absent before reporting on battery"
        default 10
        range 0 600

    config CANARY_LOW_BATTERY_PCT
        int "State of charge at or below which battery low is reported (%)"
        default 30
        range 1 99
        help
            The UPS driver treats on battery plus battery low as an immediate
            shutdown.

    config CANARY_STALE_S
        int "Seconds without data before the status query goes unanswered"
        default 60
        range 5 600
        help
            With no fresh data the board does not answer the status query, so
            the UPS driver reports the data as stale instead of trusting an
            old status.

    config CANARY_RATED_VOLTS
        int "Nominal AC voltage reported to the host (V)"
        default 120
        range 100 240

    config CANARY_RATED_WATTS
        int "Rated AC output reported to the host (W)"
        default 2400
        help
            Also the 100% point of the load figure.

    config CANARY_RATED_HZ
        int "Nominal AC frequency reported to the host (Hz)"
        default 60
        range 50 60

    config CANARY_USB_RESET_DISABLE
        bool "Stop the USB port's DTR/RTS lines from resetting the chip"
        default y
        help
            A UPS driver opening or closing the serial port toggles DTR and
            RTS, which the chip's USB serial controller can turn into a reset.
            Each reset drops the Bluetooth session and leaves the host without
            data for a while. With this on, flashing a board that is already
            running this firmware needs the BOOT button. Turn it off only
            while developing.

    config CANARY_TEST_COMMANDS
        bool "Accept the SIM and BOOT test commands on the serial port"
        default n
        help
            SIM lets a tester inject AC input and state-of-charge samples in
            place of the power station's, to exercise the on battery and
            battery low paths without touching the power station. BOOT
            restarts the chip into its download bootloader, so it can be
            flashed without pressing a button. Anything able to write to the
            serial port can then make the host shut down or take the board
            offline: leave this off in the firmware you deploy.

endmenu
